From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: qrtr: ns: retry announcements the new node is not ready for yet

DRAFT, not sent. Tested on the device (Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 5, Kaanapali,
kernel t20..t24 carried it as a y705 TEST change).

When a remote node says HELLO, the name service answers with a NEW_SERVER
for every local service (announce_servers()). qrtr_node_enqueue() drops
every packet other than HELLO with -EAGAIN until our own HELLO went out
to that node, and our HELLO is itself retried every 100 ms while the
transport returns -EAGAIN (glink refuses to send before the remote has
queued intents). The announcements are not retried, so a service that
was registered before the remote came up is never announced to it.

On Kaanapali the modem's HELLO arrives before the modem accepts ours, so
with rmtfs already running (a distro rmtfs.service with -s starts rmtfs
first and lets it boot the modem) the modem never learns about rmtfs,
never opens its EFS, and its own watchdog fires ~40 s later with "DOG
detects stalled initialization". On this SoC that modem error goes to TZ
without any smp2p fatal to Linux and resets the whole SoC.

Retry each announcement for up to 10 s while it fails with -EAGAIN. The
worker already sleeps in kernel_sendmsg(); announce_servers() runs from
the name service's own work item.

Before: rmtfs first, modem start -> "failed to announce new service",
no rmtfs traffic, SoC reset 60 s later (GNSS t1a). After: the first
NEW_SERVER to the modem is retried once (100 ms), rmtfs opens
/boot/modem_fs1 and fs2, 19 services on node 0, modem up for 180 s.

---
 net/qrtr/ns.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/ns.c b/net/qrtr/ns.c
--- a/net/qrtr/ns.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/ns.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2020, Linaro Ltd.
  */

+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/qrtr.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
@@ -226,12 +227,19 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)

 	/* Announce the list of servers registered in this node */
 	xa_for_each(&node->servers, index, srv) {
+		int tries = 0;
+
+		/* -EAGAIN: our HELLO has not reached this node yet */
 		ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+		while (ret == -EAGAIN && ++tries <= 100) {
+			msleep(100);
+			ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+		}
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			if (ret == -ENODEV)
 				continue;

-			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
+			pr_err("failed to announce new service: %d\n", ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
